+// While the render is poorly excited (music with few tones, for instance),
+// AEC3 does not let its filters learn, so the echo of such a render can stay
+// poorly cancelled for many seconds. The refined filter is let learn then, and
+// a reference echo removal, with AEC3's own rules, runs next to it. Per band,
+// the output is the one with the improved filter where it leaves clearly less
+// error than the reference, the reference's where it leaves clearly more, and
+// the louder of the two where both leave about the same error (what is left
+// there is nearend speech, not echo), so nearend speech is never taken away
+// more than the reference takes it away.
+constexpr float kReferenceErrorSmoothing = 0.3f;
